		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Re: URDF_USE_SELF_COLLISION_EXCLUDE_PARENT issue]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=40137#p40137"><![CDATA[
Here's the solution I settled on in case someone with similar issues comes across this.<br><br>After numerous attempts I was unable to get the URDF_USE_SELF_COLLISION_EXCLUDE_PARENT to work correctly, so I went the route of using the URDF_USE_SELF_COLLISION flag and removing all overlapping collision volumes (basically the connecting collision volumes: the shoulder joint, hip joint, etc).  I then used a combination of geometry mesh and capsule collision volumes for the remainder of the ridged bodies (chest, upper arm, etc), making sure that none of the collusion volumes overlapped.  Its an approximation, but good enough for my purposes.  If I find the time to dig into the source code and figure out what's going on I'll post a follow up answer.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=12441">MIT</a> — Sat Nov 04, 2017 6:55 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
